WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.540
The way he was taken was not the America that
I know

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.000
like our own government basically kidnapped
my dad

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.900
and it was, it terrified me.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.080
Early on a Sunday morning in late May

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.290
Jose Garcia was walking to his car to grab
a coffee mug

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:24.520
when several armed agents in bulletproof vests
approached and told him he was under arrest.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:28.800
They just grabbed me by the shoulders and
I asked them

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.920
can you please let me talk to my daughter, my wife.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.100
They said no and I started screaming to Natalie.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:42.700
I started hearing him scream out for my name
and so I ran out, like three agents stopped me,

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.520
didn't identify themselves so I didn't know
who they were.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.640
Natalie Garcia eventually realized that the
agents who arrested her father

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.580
were with Immigration and Customs Enforcement,
ICE.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.700
His arrest was part of an ICE sweep that had
picked up 162 people

00:00:58.709 --> 00:01:02.159
including at least 8 green card holders like
Garcia.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.520
And I had never expected ICE to take my parent

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.680
because my dad has legal status.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.900
Her dad was a lawful permanent resident

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.060
who'd lived in Southern California for more than 50 years

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.480
and raised children, grand children and great
grand children there.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.820
I come to America for the American dream and
build a family as well.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.560
You can actually get whatever you want when
you work hard.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.659
ICE targeted Garcia based on a 17 year old
domestic violence misdemeanor

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.480
which he says happened when a neighbor called
the police

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.680
after overhearing an argument between him
and his wife.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:44.770
The courthouse didn't retain any documents
describing the incident in any further detail.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:50.060
But Garcia's guilty plea in 2001 made him
technically eligible for deportation.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.499
At the time of Garcia's arrest, national attention
was focused

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.280
on the family separation crisis at the US
Mexico border.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.980
Protesters railed against the Trump administration
action that separates children

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.170
from parents accused of violating immigration
laws.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:12.420
I have put in place a zero tolerance policy
for illegal entry on our southwest border.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.220
And soon Garcia's case began to receive national
attention.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:21.020
Natalie found herself standing at the center
of a media storm and defending her father.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.060
They should not even be separating families.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.660
I became the poster child for this whole entire
situation.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.500
I'm a private person in general, being in
front of the camera

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.700
it was never something that I wanted to do.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.700
But the more that I was the more that know
it was helping my father.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.080
She told me she was going to get me out of
there.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:48.580
And I believed in her and I knew she was going
to do it one way or the other.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.269
The judge granted Jose's case during the very
first hearing

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:58.460
a highly unusual move according to his Los
Angeles based immigration attorney Mickenzy Mackens.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:04.599
The fact that mister Garcia's case was granted
at the first court hearing is extraordinary.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.720
I think the judge and the government attorney
were effected

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.320
by the fact that there was so much community
support for mister Garcia

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.560
and media attention on the case, I think it
helped.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.820
After three weeks in jail, he was free again.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.620
At 11 0 clock tonight the family finally reunited

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.580
but as you can imagine it's been a long few
weeks for them.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.680
When he called out my name the first time
he was arrested

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.240
it was like I was called to finish this, like
to help him

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.760
and once everything got resolved it was like
I could breathe again.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.879
Mister Garcia's case is just once example
of many

00:03:42.879 --> 00:03:48.129
where people who are members of our community,
hard workers,

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:52.980
have been picked up by ICE and targeted for
reasons that are beyond comprehension

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.760
for most Americans.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.460
Donald Trump ran for president on the promise
of ridding the country of illegal immigrants.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:05.480
We will begin removing the more than 2 million
criminal illegal immigrants from the country.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.420
Five days after being sworn in as president
he began making good on that promise

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.020
by signing an executive order directing ICE
to begin targeting all removable aliens

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.160
living in the country.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.440
The Department of Homeland Security followed
suit

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.780
by releasing a memo rescinding much of the
discretion that ICE agents, prosecutors and judges

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.520
were previously allowed to exercise in prosecuting
cases.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:32.360
The administration has basically unshackled
ICE, given it free reign to do whatever it wants

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.920
and said no group is off limits.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.720
Alex Nowrasteh is an immigration policy analyst
at the CATO Institute.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.000
He says the administration's policies are
an escalation of what began during the Obama years.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.480
When Obama came into office and until 2012

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.980
he was rightfully known as the deporter in chief.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:54.860
He basically broke every deportation record
no matter how you measure it.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.400
Now beginning about 2012, he started to roll
it back,

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.220
the deportation numbers are still not up to
what they were

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.180
for the first several years of the Obama administration.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:09.520
And it's my prediction they will never get
up there again.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.100
While arrests at the border have actually
decreased since trump took office,

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:21.720
ICE arrests from the interior of the country
increased by 30% between 2016 and 2017.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.400
Trump's executive order means that they're
basically trying to draft

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.000
every police officer in the country into being an immigration enforcer,

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.120
while also increasing the amount of power
that the federal agents already have.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.740
It's sort of an effort to roll back the clock
in a sense

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.270
to go back to the way that immigration enforcement
was

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:44.540
during the first 3 to 4 years of the Obama
administration

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:49.000
and to really go back to that deporter in
chief mode.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.560
Mackins also represents Sergio Quiroz,

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:56.160
a 23 year old man who came over the border
with his mother when he was 7 months old

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.680
and has lived in the US ever since.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:03.980
As a kid I knew I came from Hispanic parents
and a family you know

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:08.920
but I felt like I was American you know 'cause
my first language was English.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:12.920
Quiroz ran into trouble with immigration enforcement

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.800
after getting into a fight with his ex girlfriend in 2017

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.680
he says he grabbed and threw her iphone.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.180
His court disposition says he admitted to

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:27.260
'unlawfully and willfully touching another
person' which qualifies as simple battery.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.400
The misdemeanor itself is not a deportable
offence

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.680
but ICE has increasingly used what are called
detainers

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.130
to pick up undocumented immigrants like Quiroz
from local jails.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:42.940
I was in county for a month approximately
and after that

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.560
when I was getting released the same night

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:48.500
immigration came for me and took me down to
San Diego to the federal.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.240
I was just like very overwhelmed because there's
been guys in there that have been for like ten years.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.560
That's why so many states and localities do
not cooperate with ICE detainers.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.640
They see ICE detainers as a way to cast a
wide net

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:04.300
to arrest people who should not be deported.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:09.060
Quiroz is now in removal proceedings and has
to do regular check ins with ICE.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:12.580
When I think about getting deported I would
have to live with the doubt and fear

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.880
that I may get executed or robbed or something
may happen to me out there

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:20.480
cause I'm just a complete stranger, it's pretty
scary you know.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:45.500
In the same way that I think all of us would be repelled by the sense

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:50.320
that somebody was accused of shoplifting say
20 dollars worth of merchandise

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:55.540
and their punishment would be to be removed
from the country that they know and love

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.340
to be separated from all their human relationships
and their property

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:02.700
we'd all realize that that was a grossly disproportionate
punishment to the offence.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.720
And that is exactly what I'd say about this.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:10.730
The administration often talks about cracking
down on criminals and dangerous gangs like MS13.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.840
These are animals , they're coming into our
country, we're getting them out,

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.900
they come in again, we're getting them out.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:20.740
So Garcia's arrest shows just how little ICE
has to do

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:27.640
and how little actual threat from illegal
immigrants is from a national security

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.020
and public safety perspective.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:34.080
That they have to target somebody with a 17
year old offense

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.400
that they have to target folks like him shows
just how safe the situation is

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:42.600
and how small the public safety threat is
from immigrants.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:46.940
When Trump got into office he made it seem
like he was going after the cartels,

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.740
the drug lords, the gang members and everything

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:55.129
and who he's actually going after and what
he's doing he's deceiving his own supporters

00:08:55.129 --> 00:08:56.220
to be honest with you.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:01.980
And mister Trump has got to change his policy,
he's got to do something about it.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:09.180
I still like this man, I thought he was going
to do a better job but he's doing, he don't do-

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.340
to this point he's not doing a good job.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.660
ICE officials declined interview requests
for this story

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.140
but Nawrasteh says the justice department's
policy

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.740
of removing discretion from ICE agents, prosecutors
and judges

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:24.920
has exacerbated the problems of America's
overtaxed immigration system.

00:09:24.939 --> 00:09:30.649
The administration is trying to charge anyone
it possibly can with an immigration offense

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:32.760
and the maximum offense possible.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.670
The problem with this is that this clogs up
the court system dramatically

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.399
I mean there are almost 800,000 court cases
pending in the immigration court

00:09:40.399 --> 00:09:47.459
prior to Jeff Sessions earlier in 2018 announcing
that they're gonna prosecute every border crosser

00:09:47.459 --> 00:09:51.660
so the likely numbers now are probably above
a million in terms of backlog cases.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:56.620
The problem with that is that the courts are
so backlogged that they can't really clear anything.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.460
So even if ICE arrests a lot of people.

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.620
they're going to be sitting in immigration
detention,

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.060
they're going to be out there on bond, they're
going to be out there on ankle bracelets

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:07.680
so they're really just not gonna be able to
ramp up this deportation machine.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:11.499
Several prominent Democrats have called for
the complete abolition of ICE

00:10:11.499 --> 00:10:14.100
which has existed since 2003.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:18.399
In order for us to feel safer in our streets,
our churches, our schools and our homes

00:10:18.399 --> 00:10:20.120
we must abolish ICE.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:23.769
I believe you should get rid of it, start
over, re-imagine it.

00:10:23.769 --> 00:10:30.499
The abolish ICE movement is mostly just an
optical one, of propaganda and phrase and slogan.

00:10:30.499 --> 00:10:32.899
The problem is if you abolish ICE now

00:10:32.899 --> 00:10:36.360
and you do not change any of the other immigration
laws that are on the books

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:40.459
another law enforcement agency is just gonna
do the same thing

00:10:40.459 --> 00:10:42.819
they're going to do it in probably about the
same way

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:46.000
and you've really accomplished nothing.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:51.940
Rather than focusing on ICE, Nawrasteh suggest
abolishing actual immigration crimes,

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:57.060
such as illegal border crossings, and treating
such an act like a civil infraction

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:00.180
akin to a parking ticket rather than a criminal offence.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:06.920
And he advocates abolishing Enforcement and
Removal Operations or ERO, a division of ICE.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:12.520
Two thirds of ERO's arrests are for non criminal
offenses or victim-less crimes.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:19.640
Abolishing ERO would leave interior enforcement
duties with Homeland Security Investigations or HSI.

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:24.700
Which he says should only focus on violent
criminals and national security threats.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:32.459
Doing that won't abolish ICE but what it will
do is get rid of the worst parts of ICE

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.820
and preserve the portions that I think should
exist.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:39.900
100% of ICE resources should be focused on
removing national security,

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.540
violent and property criminals.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:46.820
Abolishing ERO and focusing entirely on HSI
would accomplish that goal.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:51.200
Sergio Quiroz and his mother continue to fight
his removal order.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:57.360
As for Jose Garcia, he's back with his family
but plans to finally obtain full citizenship

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.780
to protect himself going forward.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:07.970
To me this is my country and I love it and
I want to stay here for the longest I can.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.449
I want to be buried over here when the time
comes.

